\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Overall architecture of the KDS-EL framework. The dual-space design operates in two complementary spaces: DRS (green, structural space) maintains population diversity via bi-objective Pareto selection, while KER (yellow, fitness space) accumulates improvement evidence to guide elite refinement. The two mechanisms are synergistically coupled across iterations.}}{4}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:framework}{{1}{4}{Overall architecture of the KDS-EL framework. The dual-space design operates in two complementary spaces: DRS (green, structural space) maintains population diversity via bi-objective Pareto selection, while KER (yellow, fitness space) accumulates improvement evidence to guide elite refinement. The two mechanisms are synergistically coupled across iterations}{figure.1}{}}
